            <ArticleTitle>ImageJ-based semiautomatic method to analyze senescence in cell culture.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>30-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0003-2697(17)30476-1</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ab.2017.11.020</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>β-Galactosidase accumulates in the lysosomes of senescent cells of certain tissues. Cell staining with X-gal is a common procedure to detect senescent cells in culture. However, the organelle nature of the staining makes automatic count impossible, requiring time-consuming manual counting or expensive alternative techniques such as flow cytometry to effectively determine the amount of stained cells. Here we present an analysis strategy for images of X-gal stained cells which can be implemented into a macro for the ImageJ software overcoming some of the drawbacks of computational analysis of organelle staining.</AbstractText>
